Subject: [PATCH 2/6] WP-0.7, enforcement (cld-advisor's series 2, patch 2;
 built on e6298271a with series 1 applied): NO LAW LEAVES THE LAW MAP AND NO
 LINK LEAVES THE CHAIN (the seat's planted case PV13). With docs/LAW_MAP.md
 and docs/THEOREM_LEDGER.md emptied, law-map-provenance and chain-locks
 passed: each checks every row it finds, and with no rows nothing could fail.
 Each now asks what its page has held since the anchor (patch 1's rule). A LAW
 IS KNOWN BY THE BOLD TITLE OF ITS ROW: the rest of the row may be corrected
 and a note may grow after the title, and the law is still there; a changed
 title is a law that left and one that came, and is named. Measured on main:
 324 rows with 324 distinct titles; in the last 300 commits one title was
 changed, and one first cell was added to after its title, which this reading
 does not count. A link is known by its id; none has left in a thousand
 commits. Main's two tests that drive these gates on a page of one row still
 fail for the reason they name, and now for this one as well. Both gates read
 the past and join the table. The lock: four tests added to
 tests/test_nothing_leaves_a_ledger.py; on the commit before, three fail
 because the gates pass on the emptied pages. 0 of 19.

